All members are actual admissible prefixes from the same initialized source. For fixed $j$, different $w$ are alternative lawful continuations from the same $P_j$. They are not simultaneously acquired inputs. The endpoints $x_{j,0^r}$ occur along one common baseline execution. No assertion makes the other alternatives jointly actual on that execution.

